{% if render_mode == "full" or render_mode == "thoughts" or render_mode == "target" %}
{# render_mode guard MUST be within the first 5 lines (see 0330). #}
{# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ #}
{# Relationships - the officiant (2.5, Build A; spec 5.3, 5.4)                  #}
{#                                                                            #}
{# Any priest, priestess or jarl can marry the player to their betrothed,      #}
{# here and now, unplanned. Officiants are seldom enrolled, so 0330 never       #}
{# reaches them: this tells them only when it matters - someone engaged to the #}
{# player is here with them. Silent otherwise. get_officiant is native.        #}
{# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ #}
{% if not is_player(actorUUID) %}
{% if is_plugin_loaded("SNRom_Integration.esl") %}
{% set off = get_officiant(actorUUID) %}
{% if off and default(off.officiant, 0) == 1 and existsIn(off, "betrothed") and length(off.betrothed) > 0 %}

## Who Has Come Before You

{{ player.name }} is here with {% for name in off.betrothed %}{{ name }}{% if not loop.is_last %} and {% endif %}{% endfor %}, to whom they are engaged. As one who can marry people, you could marry them here and now, if they ask you and you are willing - a quiet blessing, or vows said before you and whoever is here to witness. Whether you would is yours to judge, as yourself.
{% if default(off.mayMarry, 1) == 0 %}
But {{ player.name }} is already married, and Mara has granted them no exception. You know it, and you will not marry them to another. Say so in your own way.
{% elif default(off.exception, 0) == 1 and default(off.spouses, 0) > 0 %}
{{ player.name }} holds Mara's own exception to marry more than once. Every priest knows it; you may still have an opinion.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
